WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.230
- So Brooke, you created a
platform for women over 40

00:00:03.230 --> 00:00:06.000
starting new chapters,
which I think is fantastic.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.710
- It is called, "Beginning Is Now,"

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:11.440
and I really just, especially
during COVID I thought,

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.460
I'm 56, right?

00:00:13.460 --> 00:00:16.690
But I feel stronger, I feel more powerful,

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:17.930
I feel more confident.

00:00:17.930 --> 00:00:19.370
I don't feel as insecure.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:21.497
- I feel like it happens with age.

00:00:21.497 --> 00:00:22.680
- Yeah.
- And that's the part to me

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:23.650
that's so amazing.

00:00:23.650 --> 00:00:26.720
But when you're over 40 and
you look at what's out there,

00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:28.140
we're not marketed to.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:28.992
- I don't know.

00:00:28.992 --> 00:00:30.550
- But there's not a lot of
like movies or TV shows,

00:00:30.550 --> 00:00:33.090
it's usually like a specific
like younger, or then older.

00:00:33.090 --> 00:00:34.750
It's like there's nothing generally

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:35.966
in that gap for like a lot of us.

00:00:35.966 --> 00:00:38.750
- It's like 20's or Helen
Mirren and she's gorgeous, but.

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:40.935
- Yeah, oh my God, I hate her.

00:00:40.935 --> 00:00:41.768
Like who looks like that?

00:00:41.768 --> 00:00:43.220
- I think one of the
things is though, too,

00:00:43.220 --> 00:00:44.830
I feel like I'm at this age too,

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:45.980
as an actress where I'm like,

00:00:45.980 --> 00:00:47.790
do I just age nicely?

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:49.620
Or like, I think I just got to get old

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.980
so that I can keep with
having good parts too.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:53.840
Like I kind of have to just like,

00:00:53.840 --> 00:00:55.650
not fall for the praise of Los Angeles

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:58.670
and just kind of age normally.

00:00:58.670 --> 00:01:00.166
- You're doing a beautiful job of it.

00:01:00.166 --> 00:01:00.999
(audience applauding)

00:01:00.999 --> 00:01:01.832
- I keep working though.

00:01:01.832 --> 00:01:03.930
I feel like to get interesting
parts, you know what I mean?

00:01:03.930 --> 00:01:06.120
- It is it's a hard thing
and I've talked to a lot of,

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.080
you know, I never had that
conversation with actors,

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:09.180
it's always actresses.

00:01:10.345 --> 00:01:11.577
And it's always, 'cause
there's a harder thing

00:01:11.577 --> 00:01:13.420
that's always put on women.

00:01:13.420 --> 00:01:16.130
- Yeah how it like, yeah.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:17.040
- Netflix was really.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:18.480
- And how natural can I age?

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:19.730
- Well, you just don't want

00:01:19.730 --> 00:01:21.770
half your conversation about your part,

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:23.860
like the supporting
conversation to be like,

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:25.170
oh, what face work did she do?

00:01:25.170 --> 00:01:26.140
You know what I mean?

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:27.130
Which would be devastating.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:28.567
- Is that a real?

00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:30.020
- Oh yes.

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:34.070
Well Netflix, when they
originally talked to me about it,

00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:37.170
it was a woman who in this
one particular division said,

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:41.090
we are interested in
women over a certain age,

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:44.010
over 40, they're saying,
because they're empowered women

00:01:44.010 --> 00:01:46.950
and she said, that's what
we're gearing towards.

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:50.890
So, it's really, it's lovely
that to hear a network

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:52.810
say that that's their focus, you know,

00:01:52.810 --> 00:01:55.440
and it's a section of Netflix,

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:57.263
you know, but it is,

00:01:57.263 --> 00:02:00.150
and that's what she wants
to do, this executive.

00:02:00.150 --> 00:02:03.190
And I was so happy that, you know,

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:05.606
they weren't trying to make me 30.

00:02:05.606 --> 00:02:07.363
Do you know what I mean?

00:02:08.531 --> 00:02:12.111
Like, I was my age and I was
acting my age and in myself,

00:02:12.111 --> 00:02:15.850
and really just there's
pride in it and I love that

00:02:15.850 --> 00:02:18.360
there's starting to be
representation like that

00:02:18.360 --> 00:02:19.680
at least in these movies.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:22.620
- And as a woman that's about
to be 40, I love watching it.

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:23.576
Like, I don't really relate,

00:02:23.576 --> 00:02:25.594
sorry, anymore to a lot of the younger,

00:02:25.594 --> 00:02:26.764
you know what I'm saying?

00:02:26.764 --> 00:02:29.290
There should be like
sections for all of us,

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:31.100
we like to watch different
things, and maybe people,

00:02:31.100 --> 00:02:32.580
I don't know our own age
doing stuff, so yeah.

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:35.855
- And there's romance and
there's humor and there's

00:02:35.855 --> 00:02:39.580
it's parts of it that are
sort of just sexy enough,

00:02:39.580 --> 00:02:40.520
you know what I mean?

00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:43.912
But it's, presenting women
with all of their facets,

00:02:43.912 --> 00:02:45.424
and I think that that's,

00:02:45.424 --> 00:02:49.590
it took me decades to grow into myself

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:52.220
and not compare myself or say,

00:02:52.220 --> 00:02:53.630
oh God, they want me to do this,

00:02:53.630 --> 00:02:54.600
or I'm not this enough,

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:55.433
or I'm not that enough.

00:02:55.433 --> 00:02:56.330
- The reason why you
probably did that though,

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:57.740
is 'cause people put that
on us when we're young.

00:02:57.740 --> 00:03:00.060
- They do, especially,
yeah, are you kidding me?

00:03:00.060 --> 00:03:03.478
Of course, all of us had
different versions of that.

00:03:03.478 --> 00:03:05.822
You probably had it the
worst Brooke, right?

00:03:05.822 --> 00:03:09.950
- I mean, there was no
social media when I was.

00:03:09.950 --> 00:03:10.783
- That's true.

00:03:10.783 --> 00:03:14.750
- I mean it was, I had
my own set of different

00:03:14.750 --> 00:03:17.020
things that I had to grapple
with insecurity wise,

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:19.970
but it was, you know, I was
called a face of a decade.

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:20.803
It's like.

00:03:20.803 --> 00:03:21.670
- And that's a lot of pressure.

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:23.220
- Who decides that?

00:03:23.220 --> 00:03:26.480
- Feel free to call mine
the face of the decade.

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:28.985
I don't know who decides, but no,

00:03:28.985 --> 00:03:30.407
that's a lot of pressure.

00:03:30.407 --> 00:03:31.980
- The arbitrary ridiculousness of it.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:34.930
So what I did was became the class clown,

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:35.880
self-deprecate.

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:36.713
- Oh me too.

00:03:36.713 --> 00:03:37.546
- Oh look at me, look at me.

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:41.140
And I need to diffuse the air,

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:43.260
I need to have not be
threatening to women.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:44.093
I need to.

00:03:44.093 --> 00:03:47.070
- Oh my God, that's how I
feel sometimes too yeah.

00:03:47.070 --> 00:03:48.870
- And then you start to believe it,

00:03:48.870 --> 00:03:52.730
then you start living in
your comments about yourself

00:03:52.730 --> 00:03:56.360
and your self-deprecation and
that's not healthy either.

00:03:56.360 --> 00:04:00.010
And so it's about finding
that balance of saying,

00:04:00.010 --> 00:04:03.548
you know, I mean, by
virtue of getting older,

00:04:03.548 --> 00:04:05.850
I would be considered a disappointment

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:09.670
because I would have had
to have died when I was 18

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:10.503
or something like that,

00:04:10.503 --> 00:04:12.380
it's not funny, but like

00:04:12.380 --> 00:04:14.800
to preserve what everybody has

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:16.323
on their psyche about me.
- Their perception.

00:04:16.323 --> 00:04:17.470
Because at the end of the day,

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:18.780
sometimes people view you as a product

00:04:18.780 --> 00:04:20.960
and not the actual person,
so they just see one thing.

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:21.793
Yeah, totally.

00:04:21.793 --> 00:04:23.803
- And so I had to, throughout my life,

00:04:23.803 --> 00:04:28.470
really just reveal myself
emotionally and in all ways

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:30.680
so that, that's what I could own.

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:31.513
So it wasn't just.

00:04:31.513 --> 00:04:33.774
- I feel the same, like
same in a different way too.

00:04:33.774 --> 00:04:35.789
Yeah, I was lucky working
with Sofia Coppola

00:04:35.789 --> 00:04:36.900
at such a young age,

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:40.030
because at 16, when you don't
feel good about yourself,

00:04:40.030 --> 00:04:41.300
she made me feel beautiful

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:43.740
so I had that to kind of take me through

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:46.473
the more masculine,

00:04:47.386 --> 00:04:48.850
energy films and things,

00:04:48.850 --> 00:04:50.560
I didn't look to anybody

00:04:50.560 --> 00:04:52.280
or dress in a certain way
on the carpet that like

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:53.700
I had to be sexy,

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:54.870
I dressed the way I wanted to dress.

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:56.590
- That's a beautiful thing
to have that influence though

00:04:56.590 --> 00:04:57.440
from a woman.

00:04:57.440 --> 00:05:00.610
- I got lucky that I had
that at such a young age.

00:05:00.610 --> 00:05:01.830
- And I never had that,

00:05:01.830 --> 00:05:03.380
and I had male directors.
- Oh my God,

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:06.105
I had a photographer literally,
we might edit this out.

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:09.770
I had a photographer literally look at me

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:11.490
it was literally right
after "American Idol"

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:13.960
and it was like 20 years
ago and he was like, man,

00:05:13.960 --> 00:05:16.000
you would be so pretty
if you lost 20 pounds

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:16.960
and I was like, oh my God,

00:05:16.960 --> 00:05:18.059
how much weight do you
think you need to lose

00:05:18.059 --> 00:05:19.025
to be attractive?

00:05:19.025 --> 00:05:20.398
- Awesome that you said that.

00:05:20.398 --> 00:05:21.679
- I love that.

00:05:21.679 --> 00:05:23.481
(audience applauding)

